> what is the range of x for a byte x?
  note: "byte" without signed or unsigned: read as unsigned, u8, not signed, i8 (say "unsigned byte", or "assume bytes are signed")
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the range of x for a char x?
  note: "char" without signed or unsigned: read as signed, i8 (as on x86), not unsigned, u8 (as on ARM) (say "signed char", or "assume chars are unsigned")
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -128..127   (256 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> does x plus 1 overflow for an int x?
  note: "int": read as a C int, i32, not an unbounded integer, int (say "32-bit int" or "unbounded integer", or "assume int means unbounded")
  ucas: it(x: i32) = x + 1
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  x + 1   (i32)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=-1
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=2147483647  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 1 points, e.g. x=2147483647
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
> what is the range of n for an integer n?
  note: "integer" without a width: read as an unbounded integer, int, not a C int, i32 (say "32-bit integer", or "assume integers are 32-bit")
  ucas: it(n: int) = n
  ucas: range it
range of it -> int:
  -9223372036854775808..9223372036854775807  (sampled min/max; not a sound bound)
  fits in i64
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 2^64 or more points); not exhaustive
  sound bound (intervals): -9223372036854775808..9223372036854775807
  proved bound (monotonicity, exact algebra): -9223372036854775808..9223372036854775807
  the sample reaches both ends: the range is exactly -9223372036854775808..9223372036854775807 (proved)
    max: it is nondecreasing in n, so take n = 9223372036854775807:
      9223372036854775807
    min: it is nondecreasing in n, so take n = -9223372036854775808:
      -9223372036854775808
> what is the range of x for a word x?
  note: "word": read as 32 bits (ARM word), not 16 bits (x86 WORD) or 64 bits (machine word) (say "16-bit", "32-bit" or "64-bit", or "assume words are 64-bit")
  ucas: it(x: u32) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u32:
  0..4294967295  (sampled min/max; not a sound bound)
  fits in u32
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
  sound bound (intervals): 0..4294967295
  proved bound (monotonicity, exact algebra): 0..4294967295
  the sample reaches both ends: the range is exactly 0..4294967295 (proved)
    max: it is nondecreasing in x, so take x = 4294967295:
      4294967295
    min: it is nondecreasing in x, so take x = 0:
      0
> what is the range of x for a 12-bit x?
  note: "12-bit" without signed or unsigned: read as unsigned, u12, not signed, i12 (say "unsigned" or "signed", or "assume N-bit numbers are signed")
  ucas: it(x: u12) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u12:
  0..4095   (4096 distinct values)
  fits in u12
  over all 4096 points of the domain
