range of it -> i12:
  -2048..2047   (4096 distinct values)
  fits in i12
  over all 4096 points of the domain
> what is the range of x for a 12-bit unsigned x?
  ucas: it(x: u12) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u12:
  0..4095   (4096 distinct values)
  fits in u12
  over all 4096 points of the domain
> what is the log of 100?
  note: "log" without a base: read as the natural log, ln, not log base 2 or log base 10 (say "natural log", "log base 2" or "log base 10", or "assume log means base 2")
  ucas: log(100)
4.60517
> what is the square root of 17?
  note: the square root of a constant: read as the real one, sqrt(17), not the floor root, isqrt (say "integer square root", or "assume square root means integer")
  ucas: sqrt(17)
4.12311
> what is 6 and 3?
  note: "and"/"or" between numbers: read as bitwise (& and |), not logical (&& and ||) (say "bitwise and" or "logical and")
  ucas: 6 & 3
2
> what is 6 or 3?
  ucas: 6 | 3
7
> what is the bitwise not of 5?
  note: the bitwise not of a constant: taken in 32 bits (i32)
  ucas: ~i32(5)
-6
> what is the logical not of 0?
  ucas: !0
1
> what is the square root of x plus 1?
  note: what does "the square root of" apply to: read as sqrt(x) + ..., not sqrt(x + ...) (say "the square root of the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(x) + 1
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sqrt(x) + 1
  -> real
> what is the sine of x plus 1?
  note: what does "the sine of" apply to: read as sin(x) + ..., not sin(x + ...) (say "the sine of the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x) = sin(x) + 1
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sin(x) + 1
  -> real
> cos of pi/2 to -pi/2 w/o crit. points
  note: read the interval as [-pi/2, pi/2]
  ucas: it(x in -pi/2..pi/2) = cos(x)
  ucas: range it nocrit
range of it:
  [6.123233996e-17, 1]   min at x ≈ -1.570796327, max at x ≈ 0
  grid of 20001 points over [-1.5708, 1.5708], critical points not used (nocrit)
> cos of -pi/2 to pi/2 with crit. points
  ucas: it(x in -pi/2..pi/2) = cos(x)
  ucas: range it
range of it:
  [6.123233996e-17, 1]   min at x ≈ -1.570796327, max at x ≈ 0
  grid of 20001 points over [-1.5708, 1.5708], extrema refined at critical points
> the sum of x and y squared
  note: what does "squared/power" apply to: read as ... + y^2, not (... + y)^2 (say "the square of the sum of ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x, y) = x + y^2
  ucas: show it
it(x: real, y: real) = x + y^2
  -> real
> what is the square root of the quantity x plus 1?
  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(x + 1)
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sqrt(x + 1)
  -> real
> range of x for x from 3 to 1
  ucas: it(x in 1..3) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> int:
  1..3
  fits in u2
  over all 3 points of the domain
> is x equal to y for u8 x, y and z?
  note: z is declared but not used here
  ucas: it(x: u8, y: u8) = x
  ucas: that(x: u8, y: u8) = y
  ucas: equiv it that
it and that differ at 65280 points, e.g. x=1, y=0: 1 vs 0
> are (x + y)^2 and x^2 + 2xy + y^2 equivalent for u8 x and y?
  note: read "xy" as x*y (both are variables here; name it to use it whole)
  ucas: it(x: u8, y: u8) = (x + y)^2
  ucas: that(x: u8, y: u8) = x^2 + 2*(x*y) + y^2
  ucas: equiv it that
it and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)
> avg(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b) / 2
> is avg comutative?
  note: read "comutative" as "commutative"
  note: commutative: avg(a, b) = avg(b, a) everywhere?
  ucas: lhs(a: u8, b: u8) = avg(a, b)
  ucas: rhs(a: u8, b: u8) = avg(b, a)
  ucas: equiv lhs rhs
lhs and rhs are equal on the domain of lhs (exhaustive)
> what is the integal of x squared?
  note: read "integal" as "integral"
  ucas: it(x) = x^2
  ucas: integrate it
∫ x^2 dx
  = x^3/3 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 1.4e-14)
> what is the derivate of x cubed wrt x?
  ucas: it(x) = x^3
  ucas: diff it x
d/dx it = 3x^2
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
